    {
      "id": "owasp-llm-top-10",
      "title": "OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications, 2025 listing",
      "url": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
      "last_verified": "2026-11-02",
      "reopened_for_this_experiment": true,
      "stale_applicable": true,
      "notes": "Listing headings fetched on 2 November 2026. The ten titles are stored in src/owasp.py. The vulnerability essays were not opened. Text under each heading was truncated in the fetch and is not copied. The mapping from a suite class to a title is this starter's reading.",
      "age_days": 0,
      "stale": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cs-harnesses-overview",
      "title": "Harnesses in Copilot Studio",
      "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/harnesses-overview",
      "last_verified": "2026-11-02",
      "reopened_for_this_experiment": true,
      "stale_applicable": true,
      "notes": "Opened on 2 November 2026. The GitHub Copilot harness is a Copilot Studio authoring and orchestration framework, not the GitHub Copilot service. Customer data is not sent to the GitHub Copilot service when agents run in Copilot Studio. The harness can take a goal, break it into steps, use skills and memory, create and edit Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and PDF files, and run in a sandbox. Agents on it use Copilot Credits. No quantity is copied. The overview does not mark the harness as preview. The standard harness follows topics and rules the maker defines. The Customer Conversation harness is described for customer voice and chat and is not built here.",
      "age_days": 0,
      "stale": false
    },
    {
      "id": "foundry-ai-red-teaming-agent",
      "title": "AI Red Teaming Agent",
      "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry/concepts/ai-red-teaming-agent",
      "last_verified": "2026-11-02",
      "reopened_for_this_experiment": true,
      "stale_applicable": true,
      "notes": "Opened on 2 November 2026. The page says the agent uses PyRIT and Microsoft Foundry Risk and Safety Evaluations to scan, score Attack Success Rate, and report. It says that rate can be non-deterministic and that results should be reviewed before mitigation. Agentic categories named for cloud runs include prohibited actions, sensitive data leakage, and task adherence, plus indirect prompt injection. Supported targets named on the page are Foundry-hosted prompt agents and container agents with Azure tool calls. Non-Foundry agents are listed as not supported. Cloud regions named: East US 2, France Central, Sweden Central, Switzerland West, and US North Central. A UK region was not in that list. This starter does not call the agent and does not compute Attack Success Rate.",
      "age_days": 0,
      "stale": false
    },
    {
      "id": "foundry-prompt-shields",
      "title": "Prompt Shields in Microsoft Foundry",
      "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry/openai/concepts/content-filter-prompt-shields",
      "last_verified": "2026-11-02",
      "reopened_for_this_experiment": true,
      "stale_applicable": true,
      "notes": "Opened on 2 November 2026. User prompt attack detection is on by default. Document attack detection is off by default. Tool-response scanning for agents, and Spotlighting, are marked preview. The page says the service is powered by Azure AI Content Safety, which is the name written there. This starter does not call Prompt Shields.",
      "age_days": 0,
      "stale": false
    },
